WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:04.103
HOST: Jon, Keith,
congratulations.

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.272
When you came to this
forge you used our tools

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:07.907
and our equipment
to forge signature

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.309
blades in your signature style.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:11.644
Now, we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.647
forge where you will
recreate an iconic weapon

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:22.021
from history, the xiphos.

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:24.791
The xiphos was a
double-edged short sword

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.926
wielded in ancient
Greece by the hoplites

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.961
around the 6th century BC.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.797
The hoplites were
armored soldiers

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.232
famed for battling
in phalanx formation,

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:36.468
a virtually impenetrable
wall of shields and spears.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.472
If a hoplite's spear was
broken or lost in battle,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.776
his trusty xiphos
served as backup.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.044
Much like Frodo's
iconic sword Sting

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.713
in "The Lord of the
Rings", the xiphos

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:49.949
featured a leaf-shaped profile
and short blade length.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.918
Effective for
thrusting and slashing

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.553
in close quarters combat.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.890
It lives on in Greek literature
as a classic weapon of warfare,

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.158
notably brandished by
Achilles in Homer's

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.128
epic poem "The Iliad."

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.596
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.332
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.602 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.073
KEITH: This will
be the first time

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:17.009
I've ever built a xiphos sword.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.278
Forged in fire in Greek.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:24.917
I'm going to try to put that
right on the hilt. In the fire

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.986
we go.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.688
I love working with
steel because you're

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:33.992
watching your baby being
born right before your eyes.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:36.128
The sword's coming
along real nice.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:39.765
The metal is doing exactly
what I wanted to do.

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:43.869
My wife and I are very active
in the pirate reenactment

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:45.437
community.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:48.574
And that's really where I got
my start in making blades.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:51.444 line:0%
And that's why I have the
pirate motif over there.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:59.085 line:0%
JON: Today I'm going
to do my annealing.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.354 line:0%
I'm making a container
to hold my vermiculite

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:05.859 line:0%
in sand, which will allow me
to anneal my blade overnight.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.326 line:0%
Vermiculite in sand
is a good mixture

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.496 line:0%
for containing that heat
for long periods of time,

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:13.700 line:0%
allowing me to quench my blade
tomorrow without any weirdness

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.402 line:7%
occurring.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.137
Here we go.

00:02:18.203 --> 00:02:19.806
Getting towards
critical temperature.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:23.743
[music playing]

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:29.282
[bleep]

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.189
Not even close.

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:40.126 line:0%
Didn't even get like
half of it in there.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:43.495
My vermiculite and sand
mixture was too dense,

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:46.265
so the blade fought
me on the way down.

00:02:46.331 --> 00:02:48.967
And now please don't be bent.

00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:51.203
And now I have a bent blade.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.773
My blade may not
be as strong now.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.375
If my annealing medium
isn't going to work tonight,

00:02:56.442 --> 00:03:00.213
I definitely don't want to
anneal during my day tomorrow.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.048
Way too much time.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:05.484
I'll just have to
straighten out, normalize

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:06.586
it, and quench it right now.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.824 line:0%
 The blade is coming
along real well.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:16.362
The grip and the handle and the
tang is starting to take shape.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.731
Now cutting the
umbilical cord, and we're

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.566
going to birth a baby.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.139
There you go.

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:28.708
Now I have to heat treat it.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.349
Fingers crossed and here we go.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.659
I didn't hear any tings.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:51.664
That's a great sign, I think
we have a real good blade.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.732
Baby just got baptized.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.038 line:7%
 The quench went pretty well.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.040 line:0%
I think we have a
good blade here.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.541
Excellent.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:05.143
I am a little bit
behind schedule,

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.879
so I decided to
not make the horse

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.447
guard that I wanted to do.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.651
But last night it
came to me in a dream.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.853
I have a much
simpler guard design.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.022
It's going to be straight
with some curly cues up.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.891
A little
Celtic-inspired, but much

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:21.027
more simple and traditional.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:22.662
It's pretty good.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.963
The blades got to be
finished tomorrow,

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.233
so that's the game plan.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.268
Finish of the blade.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:35.908 line:0%
KEITH: I did a little test
and dropped the blade tip

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.610
first right into the cement.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:43.049
To see how the blade would fare
against something real hard.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:46.953
Cracks the cement,
nothing on the tip.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:47.787
Nice work here.

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:54.493
Now, I'm going to
attach the handle,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.995
and then to all the etching.

00:04:57.062 --> 00:04:58.831
There is a hidden tang.

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:01.567
The tang is no more.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:03.302
I feel great.

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.571
Real happy with the blade.

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.807
I can't wait to chop something.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:10.443
We're going to sacrifice
a virgin pineapple.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.784
Sweet.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.487
JUDGE 1: Bladesmiths, this
is the sharpness test.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.456
I will take your weapon
and test its edge

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:26.091
by cutting the rope which
will release the sandbags

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.127
and then cut the sandbag.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.995
Let's see how sharp
your blades are.

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:30.963
Jon, you're up first.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:31.864
You ready?

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:32.398
 Ready to go.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:36.736
[music playing]

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.920
JUDGE 1: OK Jon.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.489
This side is very sharp.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:59.826
And the other side is sharp,
but to get through the rope

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.327
it took three cuts.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:05.164
The balance overall of
the sword feels good.

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:07.199
This sir, will cut.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.101
 Thanks.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.134
JUDGE 1: Good job.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:10.202
Keith you're up, you ready?

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:10.902
 Yes, sir.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:14.507
[music playing]

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.389
 That was cool.

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:32.358
JUDGE 1: All right,
Keith, your blade

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:34.960
required two slices to
cut through the rope,

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.462
but it did cut through.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:40.432
And then on the backhand slice,
cut nicely on the sandbag.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.968
Like the guard, I
like the details

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:43.469
that you put into your blade.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:47.606
This sir, will cut.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.008
JUDGE 2: Gentlemen, to test
the strength of your weapons

00:06:50.108 --> 00:06:53.712
I'm going to take two blows
on either side of this helmet.

00:06:53.812 --> 00:06:55.848
See how your weapons hold up.

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:56.682
Jon you're up first.

00:06:56.783 --> 00:06:58.216
Are you ready?

00:06:58.283 --> 00:06:59.084
 I guess so.

00:06:59.151 --> 00:06:59.818
JUDGE 2: OK.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:03.489
[music playing]

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:15.233
 Not a mark on the blade.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.069
Very nicely done with that.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:20.539
One thing I did notice, we just
got a little loose down here.

00:07:20.605 --> 00:07:22.641
Right there in your
guard and your pommel.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:27.346
It's not terrible, but
there's a little movement.

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.381
But you've got a very
strong blade here.

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:30.282
 Thank you.

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:31.750
JUDGE 2: Nicely done.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.986
So Keith, you're up, you ready?

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:34.854
 Aye.

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.122
JUDGE 2: All right.

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:39.992
[music playing]

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:52.738
JUDGE 2: It held up well.

00:07:52.804 --> 00:07:57.309
I like your handle a lot,
it's contoured to my hand.

00:07:57.375 --> 00:07:59.145
All and all really nicely done.

00:08:03.682 --> 00:08:04.783
HOST: Bladesmiths.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:07.086
The judges have made
a final decision.

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:10.189
Jon, Keith, in this final
round of competition

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:13.493
you've both delivered
exactly what we asked for.

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:16.562
But there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.801
Keith, congratulations.

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:24.970
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:28.441
Jon, unfortunately your
weapon did not make the cut.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:32.010
Jon, your blade did very
well on the strength test.

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:34.279
The issue we found was
in the fit and finish

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:35.714
of your handle construction.

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:38.918 line:0%
Your pommel, either it
came loose or it was loose.

00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:40.853 line:0%
And there was some gapping
that we could see through it.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.155 line:0%
And it's for this reason,
we have to let you go.

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:44.456
 Understood.

00:08:44.523 --> 00:08:47.993
HOST: Jon, please
surrender your weapon.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:51.030
I've had a great time, and
I've learned more about myself

00:08:51.097 --> 00:08:54.033
and bladesmithing than I have
at any other point in my life.

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:57.135
$10,000 would've been nice,
but I can go earn that $10,000

00:08:57.235 --> 00:08:58.971
grand with what I've learned.

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.705
I may not be the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:00.805 --> 00:09:03.776
but I definitely won best hair.

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:05.544
 Well, Keith, at
least you didn't

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:07.813
get all dressed up for nothing.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.815
You're our new "Forged in
Fire" champion, and will be

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:13.819
receiving a check for $10,000.

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:15.187
 Oh my gosh.

00:09:15.253 --> 00:09:18.724
I just want to jump up and down
and scream, "yay, I did it!"

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:21.460
"Forged in Fire"
champion, life doesn't

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:22.360
get much better than that.

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:26.098
[music playing]

